#: ui/pages.slint:2022
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Browser extension"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2023
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Fills and saves your logins in Chrome and Edge, and suggests strong "
"passwords made here. Passwords are shown, copied and filled one at a time, "
"through the item lock."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2024
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"The extension keeps no passwords. The first time, it asks to be connected "
"and this app asks for your master password; after that only that extension "
"gets answers, only while the vault is open, only for the exact site a login "
"was saved for (write *.example.com as the website to include every site "
"under it), and only on pages with https. A login behind the item lock is "
"opened for one fill, show or copy by Windows Hello or by its PIN, typed in "
"the extension's own window. Copies are made by this app, out of clipboard "
"history. Each fill shows a notice here. Limit: a malicious program already "
"running under your Windows account could copy the browser's data and ask "
"like the extension, which is why the accounts that matter belong behind the "
"item lock."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2026
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Let the browser extension ask this app for logins"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2034
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Fill with Windows Hello while the vault is locked"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2041
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"The app keeps the passwords of your logins for the extension in a file only "
"Windows Hello opens, so a locked vault can still fill: each password asks "
"for your face, fingerprint or Windows PIN. The item lock's PIN does not work "
"here, because a copied file could be tried against every PIN away from this "
"app. It needs Windows Hello on in Item lock and the app running (closed to "
"the notification area is fine). Usernames and websites stay readable to your "
"Windows account so the extension can list them."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2049
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "An extension is connected to this vault."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2056
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Disconnect"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2061
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"To install it: open chrome://extensions (or edge://extensions), turn on "
"Developer mode, choose “Load unpacked” and pick the “extension” folder "
"of this project."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2070
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Item lock"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2071
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"A second check before an open vault shows passwords, codes and hidden "
"fields. Names, usernames and websites stay visible so you can find the "
"account."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2072
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"With a PIN or another password, the locked secrets are also encrypted with a "
"key that only that PIN or password opens: a program that reads the open "
"vault from your computer's memory still can't read items that are locked. A "
"4-digit PIN has only 10,000 combinations, and such a program could try them "
"all in a few hours, so use 6 to 8 digits or a password for real strength. "
"With the master password as the check nothing extra is encrypted; it only "
"stops someone at your unlocked computer. One right answer opens every locked "
"item for 5 minutes, or until you click Lock. After 5 wrong tries the whole "
"vault locks. A forgotten PIN is replaced here, with your master password."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2074
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "PIN"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2074
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "Another password"
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2078
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid "A check only: nothing extra is encrypted."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2079
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Locked secrets are encrypted, and only the PIN opens them. If you forget "
"both the PIN and your master password, they can't be recovered, not even "
"with the Recovery Key."
msgstr ""

#: ui/pages.slint:2080
msgctxt "SettingsPage"
msgid ""
"Locked secrets are encrypted, and only this password opens them. If you "
"forget both it and your master password, they can't be recovered, not even "
"with the Recovery Key."
msgstr ""

